{
  "0": "Across all four categories, add a learned projection of log1p(cumulative nonpadding prefix length)/log1p(64) to each historical input, keeping padding zero. This causal feature distinguishes short from established contexts without repeat counts. Jointly set maxlen=64, blocks=6, dropout=0.15 and LR=8e-4: shorter inputs fund six convolution blocks, while moderate dropout and a lower LR help retain the new length signal. Preserve item embeddings, convolution formulas, scoring and pointwise loss. Use one checkpoint/category, seed 42, 200 batches/epoch and at most 200 epochs; update predictor metadata and writer consistently.",
  "1": "Across all four categories, project a training-only log-frequency feature, centered and standardized over items, into historical inputs without changing candidate embeddings. Replace each convolution block's second transformation with a causal GLU producing content and gates, retaining its residual path. Jointly use maxlen=64, six blocks, dropout=0.2 and LR=6e-4. Frequency supplies reliability information that the jointly trained gates can selectively admit; the shorter window offsets gate computation and the lower LR stabilizes gating. Preserve tied item embeddings, readout and pointwise loss. Save feature buffers and matching predictor architecture; retain one model/category and fixed seeds and training caps.",
  "2": "Across all four categories, add a projected causal prefix-mean log-frequency feature computed from training-only item counts. For embedding representation, initialize the tied item table with Normal(0,0.02), retaining a zero padding row, to remove vocabulary-size-dependent Xavier scale. For architecture, add a learned identity-initialized bilinear projection of encoded states before all target dot products. Jointly set maxlen=64, four blocks, dropout=0.1 and LR=5e-4. Prefix context and bilinear compatibility provide adaptability while the shallower backbone and lower LR control cost and scale drift. Preserve pointwise loss and final-real-position readout; serialize all changes in one model/category with matching predictor code and fixed training caps.",
  "3": "Across all four categories, construct the causal feature log1p(training_count[item]) minus its cumulative mean over the observed prefix; project this scalar into historical inputs, with padding zero. Within each existing NextItNet block, replace the residual update with residual+sigmoid(W*norm(residual)+b)*y, using a jointly trained channel gate initialized with b=2. Relative frequency highlights shifts between common and niche items, while gates allow context-dependent convolution updates rather than uniformly halving residuals, which regressed. Preserve all existing hyperparameters, embeddings, scoring, readout and pointwise loss. Save training-count buffers and update the predictor writer; retain one checkpoint/category and fixed seeds and caps."
}
